# Copy this file to `.env` and adjust for your network.
#
# Defaults (docker-compose.yml): Docker Hub images (prom/prometheus,
# grafana/grafana, oliver006/redis_exporter, nvidia/dcgm-exporter) plus
# gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor.
#
# Registry access varies by network. Two layers of help:
#   1. `registry-mirrors` in Docker Desktop -> Settings -> Docker Engine:
#        "registry-mirrors": ["https://docker.m.daocloud.io"]
#      This covers Docker Hub images only.
#   2. Image-name overrides below, for gcr.io / nvcr.io (not covered by
#      registry-mirrors). DaoCloud publishes per-registry mirrors:
#      gcr.m.daocloud.io, ghcr.m.daocloud.io, quay.m.daocloud.io, nvcr.m.daocloud.io
#
# Verified working tags (2026-10): nvidia/dcgm-exporter:4.6.1-4.8.4 (DCGM 4.6.1
# + exporter 4.8.4, the tested pair) and 4.8.4. Older 3.x tags are not
# published on Docker Hub; they exist on nvcr.io as e.g.
# nvcr.io/nvidia/k8s/dcgm-exporter:3.3.7-3.5.0.

## Restricted-network overrides (uncomment into `.env` as needed)

# gcr.io is not covered by registry-mirrors. Choose per network:
#   mainland China:   CADVISOR_IMAGE=gcr.m.daocloud.io/cadvisor/cadvisor:latest
#   overseas / cloud: CADVISOR_IMAGE=gcr.io/cadvisor/cadvisor:latest
# The China mirror can be unavailable from overseas cloud regions (observed on
# an Aliyun Hong Kong host), so use the direct registry there.
# CADVISOR_IMAGE=gcr.m.daocloud.io/cadvisor/cadvisor:latest

# Docker Hub images work through registry-mirrors; override explicitly only
# if you prefer a mirror prefix:
# PROMETHEUS_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/prom/prometheus:latest
# GRAFANA_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/grafana/grafana:latest
# REDIS_EXPORTER_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/oliver006/redis_exporter:latest

# DCGM exporter alternatives (pick one that resolves for your network):
# DCGM_EXPORTER_IMAGE=nvidia/dcgm-exporter:4.6.1-4.8.4
# DCGM_EXPORTER_IMAGE=docker.m.daocloud.io/nvidia/dcgm-exporter:4.6.1-4.8.4
# DCGM_EXPORTER_IMAGE=nvcr.m.daocloud.io/nvidia/k8s/dcgm-exporter:4.6.1-4.8.4

## Cloud deployment (docker-compose.cloud.yml only)

# Domain pointed at the VM's public IP (Caddy obtains a Let's Encrypt
# certificate automatically). Leave unset / localhost to serve plain HTTP.
# DOMAIN=demo.example.com

# Public URL used for Grafana's root URL (GF_SERVER_ROOT_URL). Match DOMAIN.
# CLOUD_URL=https://demo.example.com

# Grafana admin password for the cloud deployment.
# GRAFANA_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me

